Classify the topic of the following title of a debate from the European Parliament. 

**Title:** {{ title }}

Rules for the classification:
1. Select the one or multiple best matching topics. Use the below list of topic names and typical issues. 
2. The opening speech of the debate is given to make a grounded decision. Focus on the central topics of the debate. Assign multiple topics if the central topics touch multiple areas, or if the speech touches multiple issues independently, for example in state of the union addresses. 
3. Topics concerning EU countries count as domestic affairs. International affairs and foreign trade only concern non-EU countries. 
4. For EU membership and expansion, use 1900.
5. Avoid redundancy, if multiple facets are already covered by one topic. For example, agriculture covers agricultural foreign trade, so foreign-trade is redundant. Foreign-trade covers international relations, and so on. 
6. Only output the topic codes, separated by comma.


